.TH MUST-GATHER-SOS 1 "2026-10-16" "must-gather-sos 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
must-gather-sos \- sos-style plugin selection for \fBoc adm must-gather\fR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B must-gather-sos
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B must-gather-sos
.B \-\-list\-plugins
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oc adm must-gather
is all\-or\-nothing: its default entrypoint runs a base
.B oc adm inspect
pass plus roughly twenty\-five
.B gather_*
scripts, and the only supported alternative is running exactly one of them by
hand with
.BR "oc adm must-gather -- /usr/bin/gather_audit_logs" .
.PP
.B must-gather-sos
adds the selection vocabulary that
.BR sos-report (1)
has long had for hosts. It generates a collection script covering just the
plugins you asked for, hands it to
.B oc adm must-gather
and leaves the result in the same directory layout
.B oc
would have produced, plus a
.B manifest.json
describing the run.
.PP
Plugins are named after the upstream scripts with the
.B gather_
prefix removed, so
.B /usr/bin/gather_audit_logs
is the
.B audit_logs
plugin. One extra, synthetic plugin named
.B core
stands for the base
.B oc adm inspect
pass that upstream performs inline; it is enabled by default, and
.B \-o
selections that omit it get no base inspect at all.
.PP
The run is also given the shape
.BR sos-report (1)
has: the plan is announced before anything starts, each task reports
.I [n/total]
as it finishes, its own output goes to
.I <output>/task\-logs/<name>.log
rather than into the shared stream, and a summary at the end separates what
collected something
.RB ( ok )
from what ran cleanly with nothing to collect
.RB ( no-op ),
what exited non\-zero
.RB ( failed ),
and what the image does not carry at all
.RB ( missing ,
meaning the catalog and the image are from different releases). Every
.B TASK_HEARTBEAT
seconds \(em set in the generated script, 30 by default, 0 to disable \(em the
run says what is still going, so a slow plugin does not read as a hang.
.B \-\-print\-script
shows the value, and the script it prints can be edited and run with the
command
.B \-\-print\-command
gives you.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Plugin selection
.TP
.B \-\-list\-catalogs
List the built-in plugin catalogs, how many plugins each has, and the image
references each describes, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-plugins
List the available plugins, which are on by default, and what options each
accepts. Combine with \fB\-\-format json\fR for machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-plugin\-names
Print bare plugin names, one per line. Used by the shell completions.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-plugin\-options
Print bare \fIplugin.option\fR keys, one per line.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-only\-plugins " \fILIST\fR"
Run only these plugins. Cannot be combined with \fB\-n\fR or \fB\-e\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-skip\-plugins " \fILIST\fR"
Run the default set except these.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-enable\-plugins " \fILIST\fR"
Additionally run these plugins, which are off by default.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all\-plugins
Run every plugin. Plugins that refuse to start without a \fB\-k\fR option, and
plugins that re\-run the entire default gather, are left out; the command says
which and why.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-plugin\-option " \fIPLUG.OPT=VAL\fR"
Set a plugin option; repeatable. Boolean options accept \fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR and
may be given bare. Repeatable options such as \fBmetrics.match\fR take their
value verbatim, so a value containing commas or spaces stays one value.
.SS Collection
.TP
.B \-\-since " \fIDURATION\fR"
Only collect logs newer than e.g. \fB5m\fR or \fB2h\fR. Passed to
.BR oc ,
which sets \fBMUST_GATHER_SINCE\fR in the pod; the generated script sources
\fB/usr/bin/common.sh\fR so plugins that support a time window honour it.
See \fBTHE REACH OF \-\-SINCE\fR below: it is not universal.
.TP
.B \-\-since\-time " \fIRFC3339\fR"
Only collect logs after a specific time, e.g. \fB2026\-10\-16T09:00:00Z\fR.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-since\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-reduce\-logs " \fILIST\fR"
Comma separated, any of \fBskip_rotated_logs\fR, \fBcompress_service_logs\fR,
\fBcompress_logs\fR. Exported as \fBREDUCE_LOGS\fR for \fBcommon.sh\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Most collection scripts to run at once inside the pod, the way
.BR sos-report (1)
uses \fB\-\-threads\fR. \fB0\fR, the default, is unlimited \(em what
upstream's \fBgather\fR does. Use it when a cluster cannot take two dozen
\fBoc adm inspect\fR calls arriving together. Written into the generated
script as \fBTASK_JOBS\fR, so \fB\-\-print\-script\fR shows it; a task
waiting for a slot has not started, and so is neither reported as running
nor charged for the wait.
.SS Output
.TP
.B \-\-dest\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Write gathered data here. Defaults to \fBmust\-gather.local.\fIRAND\fR in the
current directory, matching \fBoc\fR's own naming.
.TP
.B \-\-case\-id " \fIID\fR"
Support case number. Recorded in \fBmanifest.json\fR and used in the archive
name.
.TP
.BR \-\-archive " [\fIFORMAT\fR]"
Tar up the result. \fIFORMAT\fR is \fBxz\fR (the default), \fBgz\fR or
\fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-manifest
Do not write \fBmanifest.json\fR into the output.
.SS Passed through to oc adm must\-gather
.B \-\-image\fR,
.B \-\-image\-stream\fR,
.B \-\-timeout\fR,
.B \-\-node\-name\fR,
.B \-\-node\-selector\fR,
.B \-\-run\-namespace\fR,
.B \-\-host\-network\fR,
.B \-\-volume\-percentage\fR,
.BR \-\-source\-dir .
Only one \fB\-\-image\fR is accepted, because the catalog describes a single
image's plugin layout.
.SS Behaviour
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the generated in\-pod script and the \fBoc\fR command, and run nothing.
Needs no cluster.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-command
Print only the full \fBoc\fR command, shell\-quoted and ready to paste, then
exit. Needs no cluster.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-script
Print only the generated in\-pod script, then exit. Needs no cluster.
.TP
.B \-\-batch
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog " [\fIIMAGE\fR=]\fINAME\fR|\fIPATH\fR"
Use a different plugin catalog: a built-in name (see
\fB\-\-list\-catalogs\fR) or a path to one of your own. With several
images, prefix it with the image it describes. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-oc " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to the \fBoc\fR binary.
.SH SEVERAL IMAGES
.B \-\-image
is repeatable, as it is for
.BR "oc adm must-gather" .
Each image needs a catalog, chosen by matching the image reference against
the patterns in
.BR \-\-list\-catalogs ;
pin one explicitly with \fB\-\-catalog IMAGE=NAME\fR. Plugin selection
(\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-n\fR, \fB\-e\fR, \fB\-k\fR) is global: a name must exist in
some selected catalog, and does not apply to the images that lack it. An
image left with nothing selected is dropped from the run.
.PP
It is still one
.B oc
invocation.
.B oc
joins everything after \fB\-\-\fR into a single string and gives that same
string to every image's pod, so the generated script carries a branch per
image family and detects at run time which one it is in \(em
\fB\-\-print\-script\fR shows the whole thing. Each pod writes a
\fBmust\-gather\-sos\-profile\fR file naming the branch it took, because
\fBoc\fR names its output directories after the resolved image digest, which
cannot be known in advance. An image no catalog recognises runs its own
entrypoint, which is what plain \fBoc adm must-gather\fR would have done.
.PP
Two pods' progress lines interleave in the live stream; \fBoc\fR prefixes
each with the pod name, and every pod still writes its own
\fBgather\-progress.log\fR and \fBtask\-logs/\fR.
.PP
Red Hat ACM is supported through the \fBacm\fR catalog. Note that
\fB\-\-since\fR and \fB\-\-reduce\-logs\fR do nothing against it: the ACM
image has no \fBcommon.sh\fR and never reads \fBMUST_GATHER_SINCE\fR, which
\fBmust-gather-sos\fR says once rather than per plugin. ACS is not
supported; there is no official ACS must-gather image, and the documented
route is \fBroxctl central debug download\-diagnostics\fR.
.SH THE REACH OF \-\-SINCE
\fB\-\-since\fR and \fB\-\-since\-time\fR change what is collected in exactly
two places. This is an upstream limitation, not one this tool adds.
.TP
.B oc adm inspect \-\-since
Trims \fBpod logs\fR. Applies to \fBcore\fR and thirteen other plugins.
.TP
.B oc adm node-logs \-\-since " on a journal query"
Trims \fBhost service logs\fR. Applies to \fBservice_logs\fR and \fBppc\fR.
.PP
Everywhere else the window is accepted and has no effect. One case deserves
spelling out, because it looks like it should work.
.B gather_audit_logs
\fIdoes\fR support \fB\-\-since\fR: it sources \fBcommon.sh\fR, calls
\fBget_log_collection_args\fR and threads \fBnode_log_collection_args\fR into
both of its \fBoc adm node-logs\fR calls. The plugin is not at fault. The two
layers beneath it are:
.IP \(bu 3
.B oc
does not send it.
.B oc adm node-logs
attaches the \fBsince\fR parameter only when the path is \fBjournal\fR
(\fIpkg/cli/admin/node/logs.go\fR in openshift/oc); the flag help reads
"Only applies to node service logs".
.IP \(bu 3
The kubelet would not honour it anyway. Asked directly it \fIvalidates\fR the
parameter but does not time\-filter plain file serving.
.PP
Measured on a 4.18.54 cluster: a rotated audit file returned 134269 lines,
first event 11 hours before the cutoff, identically with no parameter, with
\fB?since=\-5m\fR, with \fB?since=\-1h\fR and with
\fB?since=2026\-10\-16 06:00:00\fR.
.PP
So \fBaudit_logs\fR, \fBkas_startup_termination_logs\fR and
\fBwindows_node_logs\fR always return whole files. Plugins that copy files out
of pods, or query Prometheus, have no window either.
.PP
.B must-gather-sos
warns before it runs when a selected plugin cannot act on the window, and
\fB\-\-list\-plugins\fR annotates every plugin with what \fB\-\-since\fR does
to it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Everything the default gather does, as a baseline:
.PP
.RS
.B must-gather-sos
.RE
.PP
The defaults minus two noisy plugins, last two hours only:
.PP
.RS
.B must-gather-sos \-n monitoring,istio \-\-since 2h
.RE
.PP
Only etcd and SR\-IOV, with the base inspect pass:
.PP
.RS
.B must-gather-sos \-o core,etcd,sriov
.RE
.PP
Audit logs even though the audit profile is None:
.PP
.RS
.B must-gather-sos \-o audit_logs \-k audit_logs.force=on \-\-since 30m
.RE
.PP
A bundle to attach to a support case:
.PP
.RS
.B must-gather-sos \-o core,etcd \-\-case\-id 04123456 \-\-archive
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I must_gather_sos/data/openshift.json
The vendored plugin catalog, generated from openshift/must\-gather by
\fBtools/sync_catalog.py\fR.
.TP
.I must_gather_sos/data/task_common.sh
The sos\-style progress library, inlined into the generated script because
the image has no copy of it.
.TP
.I <output>/manifest.json
What ran, with what options, against which cluster, and each plugin's state,
exit status and duration, with a tally by state.
.TP
.I <output>/must-gather-sos-script.sh
A copy of the script that ran inside the pod.
.TP
.I <output>/must-gather-sos-profile
Which image family wrote this directory, when a run covered several.
.TP
.I <output>/must-gather-sos-plugins.log
Raw per\-plugin results written in the pod, tab separated: name, state, exit
code, seconds, detail.
.TP
.I <output>/gather-progress.log
The progress as it was printed, without \fBoc\fR's disk\-usage checker
interleaved through it.
.TP
.I <output>/task-logs/<name>.log
Everything one task printed, kept out of the shared stream.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A problem with the request, reported without a traceback.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.PP
Any other value is \fBoc\fR's own exit code, passed through. Note that
individual plugin failures do not change the exit status; check the summary
printed at the end, or \fBmanifest.json\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oc (1),
.BR sos-report (1)
.PP
